    "policy_hash": "cf89ad9eddd6cf458f3e06c101b10c2c762814fe62b9e36d4149dfcb7a53f9c1",
    "policy_notes": [
      "Validated workflow specification GIRAFFE under project policy cf89ad9eddd6.",
      "The verified netZooPy 0.11.0 API is `netZooPy.giraffe.Giraffe(expression, prior, ppi, ...)`; the agent calls only the required three positional arrays and uses the package defaults for all optional parameters.",
      "expression_file is a gene-by-sample numeric table. The first column contains unique gene IDs; a header supplies sample IDs, while a headerless file receives deterministic sample_1, sample_2, ... labels for output only.",
      "motif_file is either a three-column regulator,gene,weight edge list or a labelled TF-by-gene matrix. Its gene IDs must exactly match expression IDs.",
      "ppi_file is either a two/three-column TF edge list or a labelled square TF matrix. The adapter explicitly symmetrizes edge-list pairs and supplies the required unit diagonal; all TF IDs must match the motif/prior TF set.",
      "Missing files, delimiter/shape errors, empty or non-finite values, duplicate IDs/pairs, non-square or non-symmetric PPI data, and identifier mismatches are rejected before the API call.",
      "output_file is the regulation matrix. The TFA matrix is written beside it as `<output stem>.tfa<same suffix>`, both with a `tf_id` column and validated identifier order.",
      "The Dockerfile is the canonical runtime. It pins netZooPy to 60bcaf5ac69ac8f002db5fc6b1b10cbc101ee822 (version 0.11.0), installs patsy, and runs an import/signature smoke test during image build. The host Python environment is not silently modified.",
      "Require at least two expression samples before execution."
    ],
